Q 3142 2278 3066 2240 Q 2822 2118 2550 2016 Q 2278 1914 1894 1914 Q 1414 1914 1065 2096 Q 717 2278 534 2592 Q 352 2906 352 3302 Q 352 3757 569 4096 Q 787 4435 1164 4620 Q 1542 4806 2003 4806 Q 2554 4806 2954 4528 Q 3354 4250 3571 3722 Q 3789 3194 3789 2445 Q 3789 1664 3555 1104 Q 3322 544 2896 243 Q 2470 -58 1869 -58 L 1869 -58 z\nM 1965 2362 Q 2150 2362 2348 2403 Q 2547 2445 2732 2521 Q 2918 2598 3046 2688 Q 3123 2739 3148 2793 Q 3174 2848 3174 2963 Q 3174 3187 3104 3430 Q 3034 3674 2890 3885 Q 2746 4096 2525 4227 Q 2304 4358 2003 4358 Q 1709 4358 1472 4224 Q 1235 4090 1097 3856 Q 960 3622 960 3328 Q 960 3059 1085 2838 Q 1210 2618 1434 2490 Q 1658 2362 1965 2362 L 1965 2362 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-82\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(59.90625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-89\" transform=\"translate(80.8125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_9\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(290.550855 48.574345) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-82\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(59.90625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(80.8125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p4868752c2e\"><rect x=\"35.299719\" y=\"11.088\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"121.968\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Net yearly saving ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Only 80% of 'handled' contacts are truly resolved: 2M × 35% × 80% = 560k × $6 = $3.36M. Net: <b>$2.06M</b>, about 29% below the vendor's figure.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> still worth doing, but judge the vendor on resolution (no repeat contact), not containment.</p>"},{"q":"How would you roll it out?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li>Start with simple, high-volume questions: order tracking, delivery slots, returns policy</li><li>Hand over to an agent quickly for damaged goods and complaints, with the chat history</li> <li>Pay the vendor partly on resolution rate, measured as no repeat contact within 7 days</li><li>Track customer satisfaction for bot and agent contacts separately</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Go ahead, but expect about $2.1M a year of savings, not $3M. The vendor counts every conversation the bot doesn't pass on as a saving, but 20% of those customers come back, so the real saving is about 29% lower. Start with simple order and delivery questions, hand complaints to agents quickly, and tie the vendor's fees to resolution rather than containment. Risk: customer frustration if the bot blocks access to an agent.","great":["Rebuilds the vendor's number","Distinguishes containment from resolution","Revises the saving with pilot data","Designs the rollout around simple contacts"],"id":75,"slug":"cedarline-home"}